site -- the maux website
========================

    make site            render build/site/   (needs mandoc; no image, no emulator. The
                         /learn/ lessons need the sessions `make check-examples` wrote
                         and a session of another build/full.po is an error;
                         SITE_FLAGS=--skip-lessons skips the lesson pages)
    make site-serve      serve it on http://127.0.0.1:8000/  (SITE_PORT=n to change)
    make check-site      build, check, and run the self-test that plants defects
    make site-preview    build/pages-preview/: the Pages tree from build/full.po + one zero
                         block (maux-preview.po), built --local-preview; PREVIEW_PORT=8010,
                         PREVIEW_APPLE2TS=URL (a local Apple2TS instead of apple2ts.com)
    make site-preview-serve   serve it on 127.0.0.1 with Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
    make site-pages VERSION=X.Y.Z   build/pages/ from dist/maux-X.Y.Z/ (refuses on a bad
                         bundle, a demo with no film, a stale lesson session); prints the
                         publish commands, runs none (docs/RELEASE.md "Publishing the site")
    make demos           (Mac, release time) record build/demos/; `make site` then
                         copies them into build/site/watch/<demo>/

Settings, via SITE_FLAGS='...' or python3 site/build.py ...:

    --apple2ts-url URL   base of the Apple2TS link on /get/   (default https://apple2ts.com/)
    --image-url URL      the hd1= disk URL in that link       (default: maux.po, relative)
    --repo-url URL       where repo: links point              (default https://github.com/maux-os/maux/blob/main/)
    --revision R         revision to print (else MAUX_REVISION, else git; omitted with neither)
    --local-preview      allow localhost URLs (check-site fails on them otherwise)
    --mandoc PATH        default $MANDOC, else mandoc
    --man-only a,b,c     render only these man pages (self-test)
    --examples DIR       where check-examples wrote the sessions (default build/examples)
    --full-image PATH    the disk the sessions must have run on (default build/full.po)
    --skip-lessons       build without the lesson pages (no check-examples run yet)

Layout
------

    build.py      the generator, Python stdlib only
    facts.py      every number on the site, with its source
    pages/        one ASCII HTML fragment per route (about.html -> /about/,
                  watch/fedgrep.html -> /watch/fedgrep/, index.html -> /)
    templates/    page.html, the shell ([[title]] [[nav]] [[content]] ...)
    static/       style.css; diagrams/*.svg (inlined by {{svg:NAME}})
    demos/        the demo scripts (see demos/README)

Output: build/site/ and build/site-cache/ (mandoc results, keyed by hash). Never
committed.

A page
------

    title: Short title
    description: One sentence, for the meta tag.
    demo: fedgrep           (only on watch/<demo>.html)
    ---
    <h1>...</h1>
    <!-- src: docs/ARCHITECTURE.md sec Core idea -->
    <p>...a claim about maux or the hardware...</p>

Rules:
- ASCII only. Typographic characters are entities (&mdash; &rsquo;).
- Every paragraph that states a fact carries a src comment naming a file in
  the tree. check-site refuses a missing file and a page with no src comment.
- A heritage claim (who wrote a tool, which edition it first appeared in)
  cites the tree's own man-page header (docs/man/X.1) where the tree has
  one. Where the tree is silent, a BSD man page's HISTORY section is the
  reference. Where NEITHER supports it, the page does not make the claim.
  Name what backs each row in its `source` field in site/conformance.py.
  Edition names, never typed years (check-site rejects a bare number).
- Links are root-relative ("/watch/"); the build makes them relative. A link
  into the repository is href="repo:docs/X.md" and must name a tracked file.
  Never link the LAN-only Forgejo: check-site refuses it.
- A page OUTSIDE pages/learn/ must not link INTO /learn/<lesson>/. The
  lesson pages are absent in a --skip-lessons build (a gated mode: the
  lessons need the sessions `make check-examples` writes), so such a link
  is a broken link there and check-site says so. Link to /learn/ itself,
  or name the lesson in prose. Lesson -> watch links are fine: the watch
  pages are always built.
- Placeholders: {{fact:NAME}}, {{svg:NAME}}, {{demo:NAME}}, {{gen:NAME}}.
  gen blocks live in build.py as gen_NAME (hero, demogallery, player,
  democommands, democaptions, demotranscript, demogate, ladder, syscalls,
  download, verification, gatelist, manindexsummary, tryit, builtrev,
  conformance_table, conformance_gaps, conformance_utils).

A lesson page
-------------

A page under pages/learn/ has a `lesson: lN` header. It is built only if
scripts/check_examples.py lists lN in LESSON_IDS, defines row_lN, and
build/examples/lN/session.txt exists (`make check-examples` writes it, and
nothing else does: its first lines record the git revision and the sha256 of
the build/full.po it ran on; a session of another disk is "stale"). Use
{{file:examples/DIR/NAME}} to include a lesson file verbatim, {{gen:session}} for
the gate's session ("$ " lines were typed, "[ ... ]" lines are notes) and
{{gen:lessonnav}} for previous/next, {{sessionout:CMD#N}} for the output of the Nth
`$ CMD` of the session (a page never types a gate's output twice). docs/EXAMPLES.md is the contract.

A fact
------

In facts.py, a function of the repository root returning the display string:

    @fact('name', ['path/it/reads'], 'how it is derived')
    def f_name(root): ...

A fact whose source does not exist, or whose number cannot be found, is a build
error, not a blank. A figure from a run belongs in evidence/ with its
revision, and its fact must print that revision too. Do not invent a number: if
nothing persists it, leave it off the page.

A demo page
-----------

Add site/demos/NAME.py (demos/README), then site/pages/watch/NAME.html with
`demo: NAME`, using {{gen:player}} and friends. A watch/ page with no demo file,
and a demo with no page, are build errors. The page shows the video when
build/demos/NAME/ has one, and otherwise the commands the script types.

Running the gates on the box
----------------------------

scripts/box_gate.sh rsyncs with --delete, so an untracked vendor/ on the
box is wiped on every run: keep vendor/ in the local worktree as a real
directory (not a symlink; it is gitignored). check-site's self-test builds
the lesson pages, so `make check-examples` must have run on the box first
(`box_gate.sh check-examples check-site`).

After a landing that changes a userland binary
----------------------------------------------

Both of check-site's recorded-artifact sets are keyed to the sha256 of the
disk image they ran on: a film records the image it booted, a lesson page
records the build/full.po its session was typed on. So any merge that
changes even one utility turns both stale, and check-site goes red naming
films it cannot know are only out of date rather than wrong. The films
and sessions are NOT tracked, so this is a regeneration, not a commit.

Regenerate in this order -- the same order docs/RELEASE.md gives for a
release, and the order matters:

    make check-examples demos       # examples FIRST, then the films
    make check-site

check-examples rebuilds images that the films boot, so recording first
throws the recordings away: a subset re-record done before it came back
stale again, with three of the seven freshly recorded films among the
casualties. Record last, once every image has settled.
